        "collaboration.notificationLimits": "Discord supports opted-in flight sharing events, independently reviewer-approved research and accepted documented exceptions. Evidence receipts and local results do not become scientific success announcements. Internal organization events retain their original role restrictions; no source files or precise telemetry are sent.",
        "contextHelp.group.flight": "Recording and science: what is happening?",
        "contextHelp.group.assignments": "Understand assignments, roles and approval",
        "contextHelp.group.evidence": "Understand original and supporting evidence",
        "contextHelp.group.sources": "Understand sources, permissions and storage",
        "contextHelp.group.live": "Understand live sharing and privacy",
        "contextHelp.guide": "Read the bundled collaboration guide (opens a new tab)",
        "contextHelp.recording.title": "Recording is separate from science collection",
        "contextHelp.recording.body": "Recording saves the flight. Science collection saves supported instrument acquisitions in a scientific session. Armed means waiting for a trigger; paused means collection is paused. Check the confirmed science status, source and retained observations. A button click or moving aircraft does not establish collection.",
        "contextHelp.quality.title": "Scientific quality and missing observations",
        "contextHelp.quality.body": "An operating instrument may still have unavailable, rejected or unassessed readings. Inspect readiness, source availability, calibration and quality warnings. Invalid or missing observations cannot become valid measurements by repeating an action.",
        "contextHelp.assignments.title": "Assignments and test cards",
        "contextHelp.assignments.body": "A campaign is a shared research objective. Claim or accept its published card, review the exact issued revision, then prepare a mission. Focus selects what you inspect; activation, attempts, evaluation and completion remain separate actions. A newer published revision does not replace your issued requirements.",
        "contextHelp.evaluation.title": "Local evaluation and organization approval",
        "contextHelp.evaluation.body": "A local pass describes your original retained evidence under the issued card. It is not organization approval. The organization independently reviews received evidence and decides contributions and campaign progress. Keep original results and review findings separate.",
        "contextHelp.roles.title": "Roles and separate permissions",
        "contextHelp.roles.body": "Administrators manage the organization; managers manage programs; reviewers need the permitted campaign review access; pilots contribute research. Your browser-approved desktop access may be read-only. Claiming, submitting and live sharing require their own grants. The server checks membership, expiry, identity and permission for every protected action.",
        "contextHelp.originals.title": "Original observations and derived products",
        "contextHelp.originals.body": "Original in-flight observations retain their flight, session, timestamps and hashes. A derived product is computed from retained inputs. It is not another acquisition and cannot increase original counts, grades or card credit. P06 can attach explicitly selected metadata/hash references for supported products; numerical terrain cells and point records are not included.",
        "contextHelp.corridor.title": "Modeled corridor is not measured terrain",
        "contextHelp.corridor.body": "The scanner corridor predicts a footprint from retained flight and configuration data. It is planning/model geometry, not measured terrain or proof of valid scientific coverage. Flight tracks and predicted overlap do not fill acquisition or source-data gaps.",
        "contextHelp.terrain.title": "DEM and DSM",
        "contextHelp.terrain.body": "A DEM describes a source-defined terrain elevation surface; a DSM describes a source-defined surface that can include vegetation or structures. The actual source declaration, units, date and vertical datum determine what heights mean. A displayed grid is not evidence that the simulated aircraft measured it.",
        "contextHelp.lidar.title": "Historical LiDAR points",
        "contextHelp.lidar.body": "These are genuine points from a historical source project when its original files and processing are verified. They were not measured by the MSFS aircraft. Preserve classification, original hashes, source/project, date, coordinate system, height reference, algorithm and limitations. Indexed COPC and unvalidated coordinate/vertical transforms remain unsupported.",
        "contextHelp.dates.title": "Source date and simulated flight date",
        "contextHelp.dates.body": "The historical acquisition date belongs to the source. Flight time, download/import time and processing time describe different events. An unknown source date stays unknown; the simulator date cannot replace it.",
        "contextHelp.datum.title": "Vertical datum and unknown heights",
